# Writeout

#C#Documents#= **Writeout** is the word processor of the suite. It has real pages, a Navigation pane, a status bar and a ribbon that works like Microsoft Word, and everything you write is Keydown text!

[Open Writeout](/writeout) · [Phone version](/writeout/mobile/new/)


::divider{wavy|Writeout|blue}
## The ribbon

| Tab | What you will find |
| --- | --- |
| #PK.bucket(Home) | Clipboard, Font, Paragraph, Styles (including Keydown Styles), Editing and Margin Marks |
| #R.bucket(Insert) | New Page, Table, Picture, Link, Header & Footer, Symbols, Captions, Cards & Blocks, Badges, Templates, Equation, and Bulleted and Numbered Lists |
| #O.bucket(Layout) | Margins, Orientation, Size, Pages View, Print Preview, Color Preview, Page Number Format, Watermark, Page Border and Line Spacing |
| #GL.bucket(References) | Table of Contents, Footnotes, Cross-references, Citations, Sources, Bibliography and Mail Merge |
| #Y.bucket(Review) | Word Count, Find & Replace, Comments, Track Changes, Read Aloud, Un-format and Re-format, the Annotator, Ink Drawing, Readability, Word Goal, Version History and Protect Document |
| #L.bucket(View) | View, Visual and Source modes, Pages, Continuous and Focus views, Zoom, and the Layout switch |
| #G.bucket(Help) | Help Deck, Keydown Guide and Shortcuts |

## Three ways to edit

The #GL.flag(View) tab has three modes, and you can switch any time without losing anything:

* #GL.marker(View) shows the finished page. Click to edit, and Keydown tags turn into formatting as you type them!
* #Y.marker(Visual) is the same page with the formatting controls visible, like a classic word processor!
* #L.marker(Source) shows the raw Keydown text, with colors for tags, headings, chips and code. Press #GL.flag(Tab) to insert an indent (a leading `|`)!

## Writing with Keydown

Type a tag and press #T.flag(Space), and it becomes formatting. Press #T.flag(Enter) at the end of a line to format every tag still on that line. For example:

```
# A heading
This is **bold**, this is *italic*, and this is `code`.
++R+A glossy red chip++
::note Remember this
```

Use #T.flag(Un-format) to turn a whole page back into tags, and #T.flag(Re-format) to format everything again. Tags that could not be formatted are underlined so mistakes are easy to find. The full language is in the [Keydown guide](#/keydown-start)!

## Pages

* #C.dusk(New Page) (Insert tab, or Ctrl/Cmd+Enter) adds a real page break, written as `::pagebreak`. The #R.flag(Pages) list in the side pane shows every page!
* #B.dusk(Print Preview) shows the true page size and margins, and #R.flag(Color Preview) shows grayscale or color-blind views!
* #PR.dusk(Margins, Orientation and Size) are in Layout, and are saved in the file's header!

## Saving and exporting

Documents are saved as `.kd` files. **File > Home** lists every saved document so you can rename or switch between them, and **Share > Keep a file on this computer** keeps a real file updated as you type (Chrome, Edge and Opera). Export gives PDF, Word, OpenDocument, plain text and EPUB. See [Files](#/files) for the rest!

## Collaboration and history

* **Review > Comments** and #PR.flag(Track Changes) work like other word processors!
* #GL.gem(Version History) (and #PR.flag(Save Version)) lets you look at and restore earlier copies!
* **Share & Chat** edits the same document live with other people. See [Sharing](#/sharing)!

## Inserts worth knowing

* **Cards & Blocks** adds document blocks like a table of contents, a cover page, callouts, columns, tabs, checklists and footnotes lists. See [Document blocks](#/keydown-blocks)!
* #G.spotlight(Badge) opens a picker for small labeled chips!
* #TU.spotlight(Equation) inserts math in LaTeX, drawn by KaTeX!
* #T.spotlight(Templates) starts from a ready-made layout!
* #C.spotlight(3D scenes) and Inkpath drawings can be embedded, and fonts like Kubasta and Monogram are bundled!
